{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786439999,"nonce":"ncC0KiX/My7/hoHvl+uxkd0XDvc=","message":"Done. The UI was run against `go run ./cmd/oto` on a real Postgres (schema 00039), with alerts pushed through the real webhook endpoint. Screenshots taken. Two real bugs found and filed separately.\n\n**Verified working:**\n- **The SSE header bug this issue was filed on is fixed, confirmed on the wire.** All four declared headers are present: `Content-Type: text/event-stream; charset=utf-8`, `Cache-Control: no-cache, no-transform`, `Connection: keep-alive`, `X-Accel-Buffering: no`. A browser EventSource accepts it — the badge goes Connecting -\u003e **Live**.\n- **Live updating works end to end.** With the alert list open and untouched, an alert pushed through `POST /api/v1/ingest/alertmanager/{source_id}` appeared at the top of the list within seconds: the count went 4 -\u003e 5 and the row rendered with no refresh.\n- **Durable resume works** (ADR 0010). Reconnecting with `Last-Event-ID: 11` replayed 12 onward — no duplicate, no gap.\n- Alert list, alert detail with its full timeline, **ack** (button flips to Withdraw acknowledgement, timeline gains 'Acknowledged by Dev User', the episode reads 'seen by Dev User'), settings, and the sources screen all work.\n- Incidental confirmations that this session's changes are real end to end: the login payload carries the new derived defaults (`refire_grace_s: 1200`, `group_close_delay_s: 1200`, `flap_window_s: 7200`, `raw_retention_days: 30`); the sources screen shows the source `healthy, reconciled 50s ago, every 30s` with **no reconciliation on/off control**; the Delivery drill panel is present; and the alert list's new **Rule column** renders `rate(errors[5m])` from the batch endpoint.\n- The SSRF guard correctly refused a loopback `base_url` until `OTO_SECURITY_ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS=true` was set.\n\n**⛔ THE ONE THING THAT DOES NOT WORK: THERE IS NO LOGIN SCREEN.** This issue's own 'done when' begins with 'login'. `web/src/routes/` contains alerts, alert-detail, groups, group-detail and settings — and no login route. `auth/login` appears in `web/src` **only inside the generated schema**; no component calls it. An unauthenticated visitor lands on `/alerts`, every request 401s, and the page shows **skeleton rows forever** behind a 'Stale, retry in 2s' badge — no error, no explanation, and no way to sign in. `client.ts` maps 401 to `unauthenticated` and nothing acts on it. I had to authenticate by calling `/api/v1/auth/login` with `fetch` from the page's own origin to proceed. **This should be its own issue and is arguably the highest-priority gap in the product** — the API is complete, the UI simply has no door.\n\n**Two bugs found and filed:**\n1. SSE resume ignores the interest filter and replays every resource (the live path filters correctly; only replay does not).\n2. An alert with no rule snapshot answers 422, and the detail page renders a red 'Validation failed — a rule key's source id must be a UUID' box on the panel carrying the product's headline promise. 4 of 5 alerts hit it.\n\nMinor: `/settings` alone is a 404 because the route is `/settings/:section`; the nav highlights the Settings tab on that 404 page. The nav link itself goes to `/settings/sources` and works.\n\nNot covered: snooze (dialog opens; not driven to completion), the groups screen, and killing/restoring the connection mid-stream in the browser — the resume path was verified at the HTTP level instead.","files":null}]}